<surname>Dev</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Dash</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Similar trends of pyrimethamine resistance-associated mutations in <italic>Plasmodium vivax </italic>and <italic>P. falciparum</italic></article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2007</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>857</fpage><lpage>863</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17194833</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AAC.01200-06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCollum</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mueller</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Villegas</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Udhayakumar</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Escalante</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Common origin and fixation of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum </italic>dhfr and dhps mutations associated with sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine resistance in a low-transmission area in South America</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2007</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>2085</fpage><lpage>2091</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17283199</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AAC.01228-06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCollum</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Poe</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Huber</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Shi</surname><given-names>YP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ouma</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Vulule</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bloland</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Slutsker</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Antifolate resistance in <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>: multiple origins and identification of novel dhfr alleles</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2006</year><volume>194</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>197</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16779725</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/504687</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nair</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Brockman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Paiphun</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayxay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Newton</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Guthmann</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Smithuis</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hien</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>A selective sweep driven by pyrimethamine treatment in southeast asian malaria parasites</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>2003</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1526</fpage><lpage>1536</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12832643</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/molbev/msg162</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><n